Subject: [PATCH 7/9] refactor(analytics): consent-gated, client-side GA; keep
 pages static
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The root layout read cookies() to decide whether to inject Google Analytics,
which forced every locale route to render dynamically. Move the whole flow to
the client:

- lib/consent.ts: small cookie-backed, subscribable consent store.
- components/legal/Analytics.tsx: injects GA only after consent === accepted,
  reading NEXT_PUBLIC_GA_ID on the client.
- CookieConsentBanner subscribes to the same store — accept/decline updates the
  UI instantly (no more full-page reload).
- layout.tsx drops cookies()/next-headers and the inline GA <Script> block.

Also splits the industries card grid into a client component
(IndustriesGrid) and re-marks ServicesTeaserGrid 'use client', because a
Server Component cannot pass the i18n <Link> as a `component` prop.

Result: all /[locale] routes are prerendered (SSG) again; only /api/contact
is dynamic. Verified with `next build`.
